# Infrastructure

Terraform-managed Cloudflare and GitHub infrastructure for `{{ github_org }}` ({% if backend == 'hcp' %}state and runs in HCP Terraform{% else %}state in {{ state_backend }} object storage, CI in GitHub Actions{% endif %}), designed to be
maintained with [infra-skills](https://github.com/hasansezertasan/infra-skills).

## Start here

1. Install infra-skills using its current installation instructions.
2. Ask your agent to use infra-skills to finish setup ({% if backend == 'hcp' %}HCP workspaces, credentials as
   sensitive workspace variables, VCS-driven plans{% else %}the state bucket, plan and apply workflows, GitHub Apps and the `production` environment{% endif %}).
3. Pull template changes later with `uvx copier update`.

Do not commit credentials. Public deployment identifiers live in the [Config](#config)
block below, rendered from `.copier-answers.yml`; API tokens and GitHub App
credentials belong only in {% if backend == 'hcp' %}the corresponding HCP Terraform workspace{% else %}GitHub Actions secrets, with apply credentials only in the `production` environment{% endif %}.

## Shape

Each directory below is an independent Terraform root with its own state and provider
lock file:

| Directory | {% if backend == 'hcp' %}HCP workspace{% else %}State prefix{% endif %} | Initial responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `terraform/cloudflare` | `{% if backend == 'hcp' %}cloudflare{% else %}{{ state_prefix }}/cloudflare{% endif %}` | Verify access to the configured Cloudflare zone |
| `terraform/github` | `{% if backend == 'hcp' %}github-org{% else %}{{ state_prefix }}/github{% endif %}` | Verify access to the configured GitHub repositories |

The initial data sources are read-only credential probes. Add managed resources with
infra-skills after setup. If a resource already exists, import it before applying.

## Config

Public deployment identifiers, never credentials. Rendered by copier from the answers in
`.copier-answers.yml`: change an answer with `uvx copier update` and review the diff, not
by hand, so the Terraform backend blocks stay aligned. Only the region between the
`infra:customization` comments is written by infra-skills and by you (GitHub App data,
state-transfer evidence, additional providers{% if backend == 'hcp' %}, the HCP status check ID{% endif %} and attestation timestamps); a
Template update keeps it and rewrites the rest. Keep both comments.

<!-- infra:config start -->
```yaml
backend: {{ backend }}
{%- if backend == 'hcp' %}
